{"name":"Bungee Cord","hex":"#696156","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bungee cord","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A long elastic cord tied around the ankles of the jumper in bungee jumping.","An elastic fabric-bound strap with a hook at each end, used for securing luggage."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bungee_cord"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bungee cord","blocks":[{"text":"A bungee cord is a stretchable cord made of one or more rubber strands inside a woven cotton or polypropylene cover. When the cord is stretched, the cover tightens around the core, allowing it to extend and return to its original length. Some versions, such as those used in bungee jumping, are made entirely of elastic strands. Bungee cords are often used to fasten or secure objects and to absorb shock."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Bungee_Cord_PICT6882a.jpg/330px-Bungee_Cord_PICT6882a.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bungee_cord","wikidata":"Q4413188"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Moscow_Russia_Park_Kid_on_Bungee_Cord.jpg/500px-Moscow_Russia_Park_Kid_on_Bungee_Cord.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Moscow_Russia_Park_Kid_on_Bungee_Cord.jpg/1280px-Moscow_Russia_Park_Kid_on_Bungee_Cord.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Moscow_Russia_Park_Kid_on_Bungee_Cord.jpg/500px-Moscow_Russia_Park_Kid_on_Bungee_Cord.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A child on a bungee cord ride in Moscow, Russia","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMoscow_Russia_Park_Kid_on_Bungee_Cord.jpg"}],"sounds":{"bungee cord":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vor